            <div xml:id="d868">

                <pb facs="0844" n="832" xml:id="pg832"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Moose, James/423: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-03T13:00:00-04:00">May 3, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>612. Personal for the Minister. Department’s 536, April 14, 5 p.m. The President
                    desires me to express to you his thanks and appreciation for the services which
                    you have rendered as Minister to Saudi Arabia.</p>
                <p>Your resignation in that capacity will become effective upon the day when your
                    successor presents his letters of credence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
